introHeading:
  en: What we work on
  zhHant: 研究方向
---
Halide perovskites showed that a cheap, solution-processed semiconductor can rival silicon.
The catch is lead, and instability in air. Our lab asks what actually makes those materials so
forgiving of defects — and how to build that property into safer chemistries.

We combine materials synthesis, ultrafast spectroscopy and device fabrication, working across
bismuth and antimony chalcogenides, perovskite-inspired absorbers, and nanophotonic structures.
Because the questions sit between chemistry, physics and engineering, the group is deliberately
mixed.
